# Build output from the vendored third-party exchange.
#
# The SOURCE is committed — it is what we build on, and it has to be reviewable
# in diffs. The OUTPUT is not: 14 Maven `target/` directories, 13 built jars and
# 218 `node_modules` trees are reproducible from that source, and committing
# them would put unreviewable binaries in the history of a repo that handles
# money.
#
# The upstream tree already commits 31 `.jar` files as declared dependencies —
# those are tracked, deliberately, and flagged in the integration ADR as
# unverifiable artefacts on the classpath of services that hold custody. Adding
# our own build output on top would make that problem indistinguishable from
# theirs.
**/target/
**/node_modules/
**/dist/
**/.next/

# Local Maven cache, if a build ever writes one inside the tree.
**/.m2/
